    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0136" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg62"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1669.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>, </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 29, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit to you a copy of a communication
                    of the 23d instant, which I have received from the Secretary of the Treasury, in
                    regard to a report that a Mr. Waterhouse has just embarked to Liverpool with a
                    view to the disposal of eighty steam vessels belonging to the late insurgent
                    government, which vessels are said to be at present in the above-mentioned port.
                    I will thank you to communicate with Mr. Dudley, at Liverpool, upon the subject,
                    although little credit is given by the department to the report in question.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d41-a1.xml" xpointer="d41-a1"/>
